# Only the Dear ImGui + ImPlot sources the bridge compiles are vendored here.
# ImPlot was missing from this list while xcom_imgui_bridge.cpp does
# `#include "implot.h"`, so a fresh clone could not build xcom_imgui.dll at all
# — the front-end, for every panel including the scope plot.
third_party/*/
third_party/*.zip
!third_party/xcom_imgui/
third_party/xcom_imgui/*
!third_party/xcom_imgui/imgui/
!third_party/xcom_imgui/imgui/**
!third_party/xcom_imgui/implot/
!third_party/xcom_imgui/implot/**
!third_party/xcom_imgui/LICENSE.txt

# Root-level runtime diagnostics
xcom_diag.log

# Root-level runtime screenshot
ui_current.png

# Third-party manuals and reference material: large binaries that do not belong
# in history. Keep the extracted notes (docs/*-analysis.md) instead.
*.pdf
*.PDF
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.pptx

# Generated Lua bytecode for the bytecode-only run/release layout.
# xcom_lua/build_bytecode.ps1 writes it here by default and the release build
# always rebuilds it into the package, so it is a build output, not source.
# It must not be committed: main.lua's package.path lists .ljbc BEFORE .lua, so
# a stale checked-in copy silently shadows the current source. That is not
# hypothetical — the committed bytecode/ui/window.ljbc still carried the
# pre-fix FRAME_INTERVAL_* global reads long after the source was corrected.
xcom_lua/bytecode/

# WiX build outputs. build_msi.ps1 regenerates files.wxs with heat.exe on every
# run (the component GUIDs are deterministic, so the file is reproducible, but
# it is derived from the staged tree rather than hand-maintained) and writes the
# compiled .wixobj into obj/. Neither is source.
xcom_lua/installer/obj/
xcom_lua/installer/files.wxs

# Upstream scaffolding accidentally cloned into the vendored implot directory.
# The build uses only implot.cpp / implot_items.cpp (both tracked); example/,
# implot_demo.cpp, the upstream .github/ and README are not part of the vendor
# set. The nested .git/ in particular must never be committed: it turns the
# directory into an embedded repository and confuses submodule handling.
third_party/xcom_imgui/implot/.git/
third_party/xcom_imgui/implot/.github/
third_party/xcom_imgui/implot/.gitignore
third_party/xcom_imgui/implot/README.md
third_party/xcom_imgui/implot/TODO.md
third_party/xcom_imgui/implot/example/
third_party/xcom_imgui/implot/implot_demo.cpp

# Reference screenshots and per-session verification captures. pic/1.png is the
# visual baseline the UI is checked against; the _*.png files are throwaway
# captures from individual review passes. None are build inputs.
pic/
